1
00:00:00,058 --> 00:00:01,649
You send an important message.

2
00:00:01,823 --> 00:00:03,019
It never arrives.

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:06,211
TeamChat is a messaging app for people and
teams.

4
00:00:06,594 --> 00:00:08,603
HarborCloud is its cloud platform.

5
00:00:08,986 --> 00:00:11,157
Fixing the failure needs both teams.

6
00:00:11,598 --> 00:00:15,731
But their logs can contain customer
information and private system details.

7
00:00:16,242 --> 00:00:21,025
Engineers must pick out what is safe to
share, pass findings back and forth, and

8
00:00:21,083 --> 00:00:24,009
check whether each fix actually restored
delivery.

9
00:00:24,613 --> 00:00:26,598
Relay connects their agents through Switch.

10
00:00:26,923 --> 00:00:29,024
Each investigates its own systems.

11
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:32,449
Only owner-approved findings reach the
other team.

12
00:00:33,053 --> 00:00:36,060
Each company approves changes to its own
systems.

13
00:00:36,664 --> 00:00:41,273
Then both teams test what customers care
about: did the messages arrive?

14
00:00:41,877 --> 00:00:42,678
Here's how.

15
00:00:43,476 --> 00:00:47,876
Maya reports the problem in the shared
incident channel and asks TeamChat's agent

16
00:00:47,911 --> 00:00:53,170
to investigate. Leo, HarborCloud's
engineer, replies that his team is
available.

17
00:00:53,611 --> 00:00:57,466
TeamChat's agent acknowledges the request
and starts checking its service.

18
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:01,762
In Maya's private workroom, it reports
connection failures and parts of the

19
00:01:01,808 --> 00:01:03,747
message service that failed to start.

20
00:01:04,188 --> 00:01:06,836
It prepares a focused question for
HarborCloud.

21
00:01:07,346 --> 00:01:11,758
Maya reviews the question and replies,
"Share with HarborCloud."

22
00:01:12,571 --> 00:01:15,288
That question arrives in the shared
incident thread.

23
00:01:15,891 --> 00:01:20,338
HarborCloud's agent receives it through
Switch and starts its own investigation.

24
00:01:21,034 --> 00:01:24,494
It finds the overloaded connection and
proposes more capacity.

25
00:01:25,098 --> 00:01:29,811
Leo reviews the change in his company's
private thread and replies, "Approve this

26
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:32,645
change." The agent applies the change.

27
00:01:33,248 --> 00:01:38,032
Its result returns to the shared incident:
the cloud connection check passes, but

28
00:01:38,055 --> 00:01:40,516
a fresh message-delivery check still fails.

29
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:44,568
TeamChat's agent uses that result to
identify what remains.

30
00:01:45,172 --> 00:01:48,701
It proposes recovering the failed parts of
its own message service.

31
00:01:49,305 --> 00:01:52,475
Maya reviews the proposal and approves it
in the same thread.

32
00:01:53,078 --> 00:01:55,075
The agent performs the recovery.

33
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:59,371
The reviewed findings and test results
return to the shared incident, where both

34
00:01:59,441 --> 00:02:01,090
teams can follow the outcome.

35
00:02:01,693 --> 00:02:07,835
Run the same delivery test again: 24
messages sent, 24 arrived.

36
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:12,247
Maya asks the agent to retry an earlier
message that genuinely failed.

37
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:15,799
It retries that same message and confirms
delivery.

38
00:02:16,496 --> 00:02:21,012
Both teams can see the findings, approvals,
changes, and verified result in the

39
00:02:21,082 --> 00:02:23,404
incident conversation. Relay.

40
00:02:23,497 --> 00:02:25,552
Two teams. One recovery.
